WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.500
Retired pro wrestler Dave Bautista's body
has always been his instrument, but just how

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:09.839
do the special-effect magicians of Marvel
transform a titan of the ring into an extraterrestrial

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:10.860
soldier of fortune?

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:15.780
The answer involves a lot more dental fakery,
time in the sauna, and prosthetic sheeting

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:16.780
than you might guess.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:20.300
Any artist will tell you that practice is
key to mastery.

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:21.180
"Do it again!"

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:22.280
"I can't!"

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:27.140
"You do it again!"

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:32.220
But if the artist's canvas is a person who
has to eat, sleep, and live life outside the

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:36.500
makeup chair, the best way to practice is
to make a model and go to town on it.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:41.090
That goes for Bautista's transformation into
Drax, which begins with a model of his body,

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:44.860
which includes his head, face, arms, and torso
down to his hips.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:49.280
From this, the makeup team creates a clear
plastic mold with holes to indicate where

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:52.040
Drax's many tattoos and scars must be placed.

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:56.260
The plastic mold is placed on Bautista at
the start of his makeup session, and a type

00:00:56.269 --> 00:01:00.290
of rice-paper-based special effects makeup
known as "skin Illustrator" is airbrushed

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:00.780
through the holes.

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:05.400
The result is a map of where Drax's tattoos
should be placed with an impressive level

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:09.860
of precision, allowing the artists to access
a portable, easily replicated starting point.

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:15.260
This level of precision is essential to maintain
continuity with a visually complex character

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:16.260
like Drax.

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:21.280
You may think it's easy to remember what color
Drax is, but it's honestly pretty complicated.

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:25.299
Compare how he looks in the sterile light
of a spaceship to the warmer sunlight of Ego's

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:27.720
home in Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2.

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:32.180
As it turns out, his hard-to-pin-down coloration
is very much by design.

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:35.660
Bautista's body paint odyssey begins with
a base coat of grey.

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:39.979
Then, as makeup effects designer David White
told Business Insider in 2014,

00:01:39.979 --> 00:01:44.630
"We added thin layers of browns, reds, and
greens within the base grey to break up the

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:47.509
tone and make it come alive before the final
color sweep."

00:01:47.509 --> 00:01:52.100
The green, brown, and red worked into his
alien complexion are subtle, but present.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:57.400
Infinity War and Endgame, which placed Drax
beside far more human characters than ever

00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:01.060
before, made the artistry behind his design
truly pop.

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:06.100
The intricacy of Drax's tattoos presents a
challenge: They're not quite like traditional

00:02:06.110 --> 00:02:09.610
tattoos, as they're raised and a fairly consistent
shade of red.

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:15.980
Yet neither are they as random as battle damage,
or as uniform as purposeful body modification,

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:18.160
like Killmonger's extensive scars.

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:22.440
They are, like Drax, entirely unique and entirely
alien.

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:27.720
To create them, the makeup artists use 18
prosthetic pieces placed onto the areas previously

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:30.620
mapped out using Skin Illustrator and the
plastic mold.

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:35.900
Once applied, makeup is used to blend the
prosthetics into Drax's skin, and a fan brush

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:39.780
is raked across his body, turning the raised
tissue of the prosthetics red.

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:43.540
Few aspects of the outrageous look of the
Guardians cast have presented the special

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:48.280
effects team with more challenges than Drax's
unique tattoos — and, ultimately, pushed

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:50.700
them into ever-more impressive levels of innovation.

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:55.480
After the makeup is fully applied, one of
the most difficult special effects problems

00:02:55.490 --> 00:03:00.310
rears its ugly head: how do you keep the makeup
looking great for hours of shooting, through

00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:04.880
hot lights, unpredictable weather, bathroom
breaks and meals?

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:09.280
Prosthetic makeup department head for Legacy
Effects Brian Sipe explained the challenge

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:12.500
to the Makeup Artists and Hair Stylists Local
706 website:

00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:17.440
"Our enemy is heat and sweat, and we had heat
from the lights, body heat from the actor,

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:19.820
and the muggy Atlanta heat and humidity."

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:24.080
Bautista is brush sealed with a mixture of
chemical and medical adhesive.

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:29.000
Though this is notoriously intense way of
finishing off one's look, it's Hollywood's

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:33.460
first choice, as it truly keeps even the most
elaborate looks from smudging.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:37.380
It's the details that truly make a character
design sing.

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:42.840
Without her antennae and blank black eyes,
Mantis wouldn't ride the line between adorable

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:45.460
and just-a-tiny-bit-creepy so well.

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:50.280
Without her pink highlights and facial grooves,
Gamora might bring to mind asparagus rather

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:52.030
than a fearsome alien warrior.

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:57.310
So it goes with Drax, whose finishing touches
have nothing to do with tattoos or blue body

00:03:57.310 --> 00:03:57.800
paint.

00:03:57.880 --> 00:03:59.740
Do you remember Drax's teeth?

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:00.920
Probably not.

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:05.860
But special care goes into making sure they
look believably gross, as a bereaved warrior's

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:07.300
teeth would likely be.

00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:12.040
Bautista's teeth are too even and well-maintained
to fit the bill, so a custom set of dentures

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:15.080
transforms his pearly whites into dingy greys.

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:20.200
Drax's eyes are just as impressive as the
rest of him — and just as work-intensive.

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:26.600
Tailor-made contact lenses transform Bautista's
dark brown eyes into Drax's ice blue ones.

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:31.200
They're the sort of unearthly shade you only
really see in television or movies; a blue

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:36.000
so bright and cold it brings neon lights and
phosphorescent algae to mind.

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:41.060
In addition to this unusual color, the iris
is encircled with a thin band of blood red.

00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:46.080
These shades bring Drax's gaze to the fore
of the screen, echoing the blue, grey, and

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:49.750
red color scheme of the rest of his body while
signaling to the viewer that there are buried

00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:51.120
layers to the hulking brute.

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:56.520
After Drax has kicked butt, taken names, chopped
a few aliens into pieces, and dropped a few

00:04:56.530 --> 00:05:02.210
devastatingly blunt quips, comes the final
task, and it's a doozy: excavating Dave Bautista

00:05:02.210 --> 00:05:06.520
from the many blended, airbrushed, glued,
and sealed layers that make him into Drax

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:07.020
the Destroyer.

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:10.580
On first Guardians of the Galaxy, the makeup
up team scrubbed it all off him with brute

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:11.080
force.

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:16.220
As Bautista told CinemaBlend, two days of
this treatment made his skin, quote, "like

00:05:16.220 --> 00:05:17.720
hamburger," and a better method was sought.

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:20.310
The answer was found in a portable sauna.

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:24.820
"I get in the sauna for about 20 minutes by
myself, and then about three guys join me,

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:28.040
and they start scrubbing this makeup off me."

00:05:28.690 --> 00:05:32.780
At the end of a day of shooting, Bautista
sits in the sauna, raising his core body temperature

00:05:32.780 --> 00:05:36.020
and building up sweat, which loosens the makeup's
hold on his skin.

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:41.240
With the help of steam-pumping hoses, shaving
cream, hot towels, and a silicone-based makeup

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:45.520
remover known as 244 Fluid, Bautista is freed
from Drax's shell.

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:50.420
The routine for making Bautista into Drax
has changed pretty dramatically over the years.

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:55.180
Initially, on the set of the first Guardians
movie, turning Bautista into Drax took a tedious

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:58.380
five hours during which he had to stand as
still as possible.

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:01.540
Taking the makeup off was another two-hour
journey unto itself.

00:06:01.820 --> 00:06:05.340
"They have these two sticks that they have,
and they have tennis balls on top of them,

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:07.020
and that's what I grab and perch my arms up
on."

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:11.020
The Guardians sequel saw a dramatic streamlining
of the process.

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:16.100
His prosthetic tattoos were reduced in number
from 27 to 18.

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:18.200
The sauna was introduced, and removal fell
to 70 minutes.

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:21.100
Bautista told ScreenRant on the set of Vol.
2.,

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:22.600
"It's so easy, you wouldn't believe it.

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:23.700
I'm not kidding.

00:06:23.700 --> 00:06:24.820
It takes like an hour and a half now.

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:28.440
The last one, they got it down to four hours
and everyone was celebrating.

00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:31.860
This, literally they attack me with paint
rollers all over.

00:06:32.020 --> 00:06:33.100
And it looks better too.

00:06:33.220 --> 00:06:34.540
It looks way better."

